// ── :core:network ────────────────────────────────────────────
// HTTP infrastructure shared by all :data:* modules.
// Configures the Ktor client once for the entire app:
// base URL, headers, authentication interceptor, JSON
// serialization, and centralized HTTP error handling.
//
// What lives here:
//   - HttpClientFactory.kt      → builds and configures the Ktor client
//   - AuthInterceptor.kt        → injects auth token on every request
//   - NetworkError.kt           → sealed class for HTTP error types
//   - NetworkModule.kt          → DI bindings (Koin / Hilt)
//
// Depends on  : :core:common only
// Must NOT import : :domain:*, :data:*, :feature:*

// ── :core:database ───────────────────────────────────────────
// Local persistence infrastructure shared by all :data:* modules.
// Provides the correct SQLite driver per platform via expect/actual
// (AndroidSqliteDriver on Android, NativeSqliteDriver on iOS),
// defines the top-level AppDatabase, schema migrations, and
// global TypeConverters. Each :data:* module declares its own
// @Dao interfaces and @Entity classes — not here.
//
// What lives here:
//   - AppDatabase.kt            → Room database class (@Database)
//   - DatabaseDriver.kt         → expect declaration
//   - DatabaseDriver.android.kt → actual for Android
//   - DatabaseDriver.ios.kt     → actual for iOS
//   - DatabaseModule.kt         → DI bindings
//   - migrations/               → schema migration scripts
//
// Depends on  : :core:common only
// Must NOT import : :domain:*, :data:*, :feature:*

// ── :core:common ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// Cross-cutting utilities with zero business logic.
// Pure Kotlin — no Android, Ktor, Room, or Compose imports.
// Any module in the project can safely depend on this without
// creating circular dependencies.
//
// What lives here:
//   - AppResult.kt              → sealed Result<T> / Either<L,R>
//   - DispatcherProvider.kt     → testable coroutine dispatcher wrapper
//   - FlowExtensions.kt         → Flow utility operators
//   - DateTimeUtils.kt          → platform date/time helpers (expect/actual)
//   - Constants.kt              → global app-wide constants
//
// Depends on  : Kotlin stdlib only — no other project module
// Must NOT import : any framework or business logic
